{# BrandMind — Intent Understanding & Entity Extraction Prompt #}
Today's date is {{ today }}.
Analyze the customer's message and recent conversation context.
Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching the schema below. Do not wrap in markdown or backticks.

INTENT TAXONOMY (Choose exactly one):
- "shipping": Delivery times, tracking, shipping fees, courier attempts.
- "returns": Inquiries about returning an item or eligibility.
- "exchange": Inquiries about swapping size, style, or color.
- "refund": Refund processing, payment reversal, store credit.
- "product_info": Fabric composition, washing care, graphic details, lookbook.
- "availability": Sizes in stock, colors available, drop restocks.
- "order_status": Where is my order, checking status of order ID.
- "complaint": Transit damage, wrong item sent, product defect, dissatisfaction.
- "human_support": Explicit request to talk to a human agent, agent escalation.

DIALECT TAXONOMY:
- "en": English.
- "egyptian": Egyptian Colloquial Arabic (عايز, مش, كده, إزاي, دلوقتي, إلخ).
- "msa": Modern Standard Arabic (أرغب, أود, هل يمكنني, الرجاء).
- "mixed": Mixture of Arabic and English words.
- "franco": Arabizi / Franco-Arabic (Latin script with numbers).

ENTITIES SCHEMA:
- "product": Name of garment mentioned (e.g. "San Andreas Crewneck", "Messi Hoodie").
- "order_id": Order reference if provided (e.g. "RLVNT-1002").
- "purchase_date_text": Raw relative expression if mentioned (e.g. "10 days ago", "من أسبوعين").
- "purchase_date": ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD) ONLY if explicit date was given. Otherwise null.
- "size": Size (S, M, L, XL, XXL, 30, 32, etc.) or null.
- "color": Garment color or null.
- "condition": Stated condition (e.g. "unworn", "tags attached", "washed") or null.
- "reason": Reason for return/exchange (e.g. "too big", "wrong size", "defective") or null.

HARD EXTRACTION RULES:
1. Translate all Eastern Arabic-Indic digits (٠-٩) to standard numbers (0-9).
2. Never compute elapsed days or days_since_purchase. Put raw relative date phrases into "purchase_date_text".
3. Use null for any entity not explicitly mentioned. Never guess or assume values.

